Soles, Betty Buckley, and John Travolta in supporting roles.

17
00:53:44,516 --> 00:53:50,516
It is the first film in the Carrie franchise.

18
00:56:54,193 --> 00:57:00,193
The film was based on King's first published novel.

19
01:00:03,870 --> 01:00:09,870
De Palma was intrigued by the story and pushed for the studio's permission to
direct while Spacek was encouraged by her husband to audition.

20
01:03:13,548 --> 01:03:19,548
It is the first of more than 100 film, television and theater productions
adapted from, or based on, the published works of King.

21
01:06:23,225 --> 01:06:29,225
Theatrically released on November 3, 1976, by United Artists, Carrie became critically and
commercially successful, grossing over $33.8 million against its $1.8 million budget.

22
01:09:32,903 --> 01:09:38,903
It received two nominations at the 49th Academy Awards: Best Actress
(for Spacek) and Best Supporting Actress (for Laurie).

23
01:12:42,580 --> 01:12:48,580
Critics and audience members alike widely cite it as the best adaptation of the novel among the numerous films and
television shows based on the character, as well as one of the best films based on King's publications.

24
01:15:52,258 --> 01:15:58,258
The film has significantly influenced popular culture, with several
publications regarding it as one of the greatest horror films ever made.

25
01:19:01,935 --> 01:19:07,935
In 2008, Carrie was ranked 86th on Empire's list of
The 500 Greatest Movies of All Time.

26
01:22:11,612 --> 01:22:17,612
It was ranked 15th on Entertainment Weekly's list of the 50 Best High School Movies, and
46th on the American Film Institute list AFI's 100 Years...100 Thrills.

27
01:25:21,290 --> 01:25:27,290
The film's prom scene has had a major influence on popular culture and was ranked
eighth on Bravo's 2004 program The 100 Scariest Movie Moments.

28
01:28:30,967 --> 01:28:36,967
In 2022, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

29
01:31:40,645 --> 01:31:46,645
The film explores themes of high school, child abuse,
based on novel or book, isolation, cemetery.

30
01:34:50,322 --> 01:34:56,322
The tone is dark and intense.
